    "core_substantive_disagreement": "The entire question reduces to whether Statement A is necessarily true. Camp G argues that under the formal definition of an 'ideal population under HWE', Cov(G,E)=0 is an axiomatic property, bounding the population parameter R^2 <= H^2 = 0.50. Camp I argues that 'K-selected species' (parental care) combined with 'typical GWAS data' (between-family summary statistics conflating direct and indirect parental effects) allows the PGS to capture indirect genetic effects (genetic nurture), breaking the 50% broad-sense heritability ceiling."
